BurStFin upstream license and public-domain notices
=================================================

The official BurStFin 1.3 DESCRIPTION states:

  License: Unlimited
  Author: Burns Statistics
  Maintainer: Pat Burns <patrick@burns-stat.com>

The computational R files explicitly state the following notices:

alpha.proxy:
  Placed in the public domain 2003-2012 by Burns Statistics Ltd.
factor.model.stat:
  Placed in the public domain 2006-2014 by Burns Statistics Ltd.
slideWeight:
  Placed in the public domain 2014 by Burns Statistics Ltd.
var.add.benchmark:
  Placed in the public domain 2009-2014 by  Burns Statistics Ltd.
var.relative.benchmark:
  Placed in the public domain 2009-2012  Burns Statistics Ltd.
var.shrink.eqcor:
  Placed in the public domain 2009-2014 by Burns Statistics Ltd.
fitted.statfacmodBurSt:
  Placed in the public domain 2006-2009 by Burns Statistics

The original files and all their embedded notices are preserved unchanged in
upstream/. Their public-domain dedication and Unlimited license are retained.
This file does not substitute an unrelated license for the upstream work.

The modern Fortran translation, tests, examples and documentation contributed
in 2026 are also placed in the public domain by their contributors, to the
extent permitted by law. They are supplied without warranty of any kind,
express or implied, including merchantability or fitness for a particular
purpose. No contributor is liable for damages arising from their use.

External sibling packages retain their own licenses. They are not included in
this package. See NOTICE.md for shared dependency and LAPACK attribution.
